# M / B009 — build-fix, caching, ci-cd.

C R157 OL WF-013 | MUST | Build-fix starts from reproduction and diagnosis: reproduce and diagnose the actual failure before editing, read the complete output and group errors by root cause, fix the highest-leverage root cause first; for failing tests decide whether production code, setup, expectation, environment or an intentionally changed contract is at fault; determine the authoritative contract for cross-stack failures; update obsolete APIs from verified documentation, never fabricated. | build and test repair | none stated
C R158 OL WF-014 | MUST | Keep repair iterations small and bounded: start with the narrowest reproducing command, rerun the narrowest failing verification after each meaningful fix, expand only after the focused failure is resolved, do not run unrelated build systems, stop and reassess when progress stalls and do not repeat variants of a failed guess. | build and test repair | none stated
C R159 OL WF-015 | MUST NOT | Do not weaken, delete, skip or suppress relevant tests or compiler, TypeScript, lint or analyzer failures to make verification pass (no strong-to-weak assertion swaps, no any-casts, no disabled strict mode, no suppressed template diagnostics); update a test only for an actually requested contract change. | build and test repair | Requested contract change.
C R160 OL ARC-001,ARC-008,ARC-011,SEC-005,FE-003 | MUST NOT | A build fix must not bypass architecture to compile (Application -> Infrastructure references, DbContext leaking into Application, business logic in Controllers, Angular-only authorization, HTTP calls scattered into components); preserve architecture and project conventions. | build and test repair | none stated
C R161 OL WF-008 | MUST | When verification fails make the smallest appropriate fix and rerun until green or genuine input is required; never claim a problem fixed while a known relevant failure remains; never leave the repository knowingly worse; report an unavailable toolchain instead of editing source or changing declared SDK, Node, framework or language versions. | verification failures | Unrelated pre-existing failures are left alone unless they block verification or the user asks.
C R162 OL WF-009 | MUST | Report verification state with PASS / NOT RUN / NOT APPLICABLE per area; never imply an unchecked area passed. | completion and repair reports | none stated
C R163 OL TST-010 | MUST | A temporary probe or new behavioral test used to establish correct behavior is kept covered by maintained automated tests before the probe is removed; build, compiler and static-analysis commands do not themselves require new tests. | behavioral probes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C R164 OL WF-018 | MUST | Build and test the frontend through the scripts package.json actually defines; never invent script names or assume a test runner; in CI install with npm ci and add test/lint commands only when the project defines them. | frontend builds, tests and CI | none stated
C R165 OL WF-017 | MUST | CI pipelines reproduce the repository's supported build and test commands: inspect the repository first, add stages for the actual project, do not assume a database, Redis, Docker or frontend tooling, do not hardcode one database provider into a generic pipeline, do not make an unadopted formatter a mandatory gate, do not depend on developer-machine state and keep failures visible. | CI/CD pipelines | Enforced checks the project adopted.
C R166 OL DEP-018 | MUST NOT | Do not add Docker to a pipeline or project merely because it can be containerized; add container artifacts only when the project or deployment actually needs them. | CI/CD and containers | none stated
C R167 OL WF-019 | MUST | A deployment that performs database migrations makes the step explicit, uses the project's approved credentials, runs it at a controlled point and fails visibly; production migrations are not applied automatically from normal startup. | deployment | none stated
C R168 OL WF-003 | MUST | Run the verify workflow before declaring work complete. | all implementation work | none stated
C X14 EX WF-009 | MUST | The build-fix report states the initial failure, root cause, changes made, backend build / frontend build / tests status (PASS, NOT RUN, NOT APPLICABLE) and remaining issues. | build and test repair | none stated | WF-009 requires reporting actual verification states only; the failure, root-cause, changes and remaining-issues sections are additional reporting duties. | A repair summary without root cause or changes made does not follow the workflow.

